{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1527896-the-dark-pantheon-villain-mantels","id":1527896,"title":"The Dark Pantheon (Villain Mantels)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-03T19:54:40-08:00","id":1527896,"title":"The Dark Pantheon (Villain Mantels)","content":"I was reading something about the Mexican General Santa Anna. I came across the line &quot;Most modern Mexicans place Santa Anna in the Black Pantheon of those that failed the nation.&quot; This lead to the realization that in every nation there is an Anti-Pantheon of Villains who are also powerful Mantels in their own right. Some figures like Thomas Alva Edison would have both Hero and Villain Mantels. <br /> <br /> Which Villain Mantels do you think are the most potent and scary. (To prevent the thread from bring locked we'll skip WWII).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T19:16:32-08:00","id":1528078,"title":"","content":"Well, I think <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benedict_Arnold\" target=\"_blank\">Benedict Arnold</a> might be one for the US; I imagine the Adversary, Trickster and possibly the Leader or Warrior Callings. Mind you this entire concept feels more like the Arthurian Knight character type than a completed Mantle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T15:27:52-08:00","id":1528128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1527896-the-dark-pantheon-villain-mantels?p=1528078#post1528078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benedict_Arnold\" target=\"_blank\">Benedict Arnold</a> might be one for the US; I imagine the Adversary, Trickster and possibly the Leader or Warrior Callings. Mind you this entire concept feels more like the Arthurian Knight character type than a completed Mantle.</div> </div> </div> </div>These Villain Mantels might seem that way. But remember people actually worshiped personifications of abstract ideas and concepts. Nike(victory) being the best known with the widest worship. General Arnold, as he appears in folk culture and iconography, is still more complex than Nike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T16:13:36-08:00","id":1528132,"title":"","content":"Are you intending these Villain Mantles to be more associated with Titans? Because, while someone like Benedict Arnold is certainly an important part of US folk culture, no one would actually honor him the way they might do with, say, George Washington or Johnny Appleseed. The Villain Mantle concept feels like it might work better counterposed to such Folk Hero Mantles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T17:42:08-08:00","id":1528137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muskrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1527896-the-dark-pantheon-villain-mantels?p=1528132#post1528132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you intending these Villain Mantles to be more associated with Titans? Because, while someone like Benedict Arnold is certainly an important part of US folk culture, no one would actually honor him the way they might do with, say, George Washington or Johnny Appleseed. The Villain Mantle concept feels like it might work better counterposed to such Folk Hero Mantles.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my intention. The Mantel of Benedict Arnold, Santa Anna, Mihirakula, Judge Jeffries, Robespierre, or Qin Shi Huang, would be interesting for a Titanic Scion.<br /> <br /> Just stick to people that people in the culture see as villains. But do exclude people other people admire. Example: The Greeks, and much of the West, admire Alexander the Great. The people of Iran, unlike most Muslims, regard Alexander as a monster. Jinnah, who is a hero in Pakistan, is a villain in India. Some people aren't seen as heroes by their own people anymore. Robert Clive is no longer admired in the UK, so the Indian view of him as a monster can be used with little concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-06-2024, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-09T01:02:12-08:00","id":1558200,"title":"","content":"That seems like it would be difficult to avoid, since some of the most heinous villains in history have been shockingly charismatic.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, I think <b>Dahmer</b> might fit the mantle of <i>Monster, Trickster and Lover.</i> Given his habit of seducing people, before proceeding to kill and eat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-09T06:55:27-08:00","id":1558202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1527896-the-dark-pantheon-villain-mantels?p=1558200#post1558200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like it would be difficult to avoid, since some of the most heinous villains in history have been shockingly charismatic.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, I think <b>Dahmer</b> might fit the mantle of <i>Monster, Trickster and Lover.</i> Given his habit of seducing people, before proceeding to kill and eat them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your post gets me to realize that <b>Jack the Ripper</b> would be a powerful mantel for many titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-09T09:23:39-08:00","id":1558204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1527896-the-dark-pantheon-villain-mantels?p=1558202#post1558202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your post gets me to realize that <b>Jack the Ripper</b> would be a powerful mantel for many titans.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, he was never caught or identified. He'd be a prime candidate for carrying out assassinations against the Scions.<br /> <br /> Oh, hell, that could be a great story hook! Use him as the antagonist of a murder mystery!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T11:07:11-08:00","id":1558639,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that certain people who really weren't villains have gained villainous reputations. Richard II is often seen as a weak monarch who's incompetence and corruption forced a revolt against him. Geoffrey on &quot;Game of Thrones&quot; has been said by the original author to be based on Richard II. However, there is little or no evidence for this interpretation beyond the greed of Henry IV and Thomas Arundel. Both men had acted corruptly and were banished from England for logical and sound reasons. Heck, even the future Henry V preferred his &quot;Dickon&quot; as he called Richard II to his cold and distant father. Still, there's a tyrant mantle associated with the lies Arundel and Henry IV made against Richard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}